Note: 'solve [s]' is the mean over 10 repeats; 'setup [s]' is measured once.
Note: IETI-DP iterations count CG steps on the Schur complement (a different operator
      and dimension), so iteration counts are directly comparable only among the
      global-system solvers.
      The exact solution u = sin(x)*cos(y) is not valid here (curved surface and/or
      Neumann data), so no accuracy error is reported. The 'L2 vs IETI' column is the
      L2 distance of each solution to the IETI-DP solution (the reference, hence 0).
      The converged solvers sharing one common value confirms they reached the
      same discrete solution.
